## Request routing (mandatory)

| User asks | Answer from |
|-----------|-------------|
| «можно показывать / пилот / продавать / Product Readiness» | **Product-Readiness-Matrix** (Gate, BE, UI, Demo/TE, Pilot, Edition, Sell) |
| Scaffold / AC / backend matrix | Implementation-Matrix |
| «полный банк / чего нет / trade / custody / OUT» | [`Bank-Capability-Inventory.md`](docs/acceptance/Bank-Capability-Inventory.md) + Readiness «Not in this edition» |
| «матрица готовности API / §4 / consumer / обнови READINESS» | [`docs/READINESS_MATRIX.md`](docs/READINESS_MATRIX.md) + skill `era-readiness-matrix` |
| «есть ли экран / UI покрывает API / класс NONE·SCREEN·SHOW» | [`docs/acceptance/UI-COVERAGE-BOARD.md`](docs/acceptance/UI-COVERAGE-BOARD.md) (derived; sell still Product-Readiness) |

**Forbidden:** answering sell/show with Implementation-Matrix or COVERAGE SHIPPED alone.  
**Forbidden:** treating MODULES_CATALOG DONE as edition `ga`.  
**Forbidden:** narrating Bank AC all ✅ as full commercial ABS while Capability Inventory has OUT rows.

## Closeout steps

1. **COVERAGE_MATRIX** actor row(s) for touched capabilities.
2. **Implementation-Matrix:** Scaffold ✅ only per canon §3.2; else 🟡; Pilot-ready separate.
3. **Product-Readiness-Matrix:** update BE/UI/Demo/Pilot; rollup = worst layers.
4. **Bank Capability Inventory** if scope boundary changed (IN/PARTIAL/DECLARED/OUT).
5. Sprint-Index / editions yaml if gate or sell claim changed.
6. `npm run check:acceptance` (PR: `npm run check:acceptance:strict`).
7. Skills `acceptance-closeout` / `quality-gates` when AuthZ/security or PR-ready.
8. ADR — if a decision changed.

## Status markers

- Gate: `gate[x]` · AC Scaffold: ✅/🟡 · Readiness UI/Demo: ✅/🟡/❌ · Pilot: `[x]`/`[ ]`/⏸
- **Scaffold-Green ≠ product acceptance.** **mvp ≠ UI ready ≠ ga.** **SHIPPED ≠ Pilot-ready.**
